the big day has arrived queen elizabeth  finally meets her namesake baby little  bit face to face a source confirms to  e.t prince harry and meghan markle  introduced the queen to their 11 month  old daughter lillabet diana after  thursday's trooping the color event  draped in white dior for her first  formal public appearance in the uk since  mexic she held hands with harry for much  of the time there were smiles for the  cameras cheers and a few boos from the  crowd less than 15 months after their  bombshell oprah interview  of course megan gave birth to their  little girl who was also named after  harry's late mom princess diana back in  june 2021 in california amid the  pandemic with the sussex family on the  west coast and the queen in england they  didn't have a chance to meet sooner but  we have a feeling that long wait made it  even more special she hasn't seen archie  for nearly two years now and she hasn't  seen harry for well over a year so she  would have been i'm sure delighted to  have got to see him and megan and the  queen's reunion with archie also  happened marking the first time she's  seen lillabet's big brother since megan  and harry stepped away from their royal  duties and moved to the states i can  imagine that she would be very pleased  to have seen harry i think the queen  particularly given that she's not 100 at  the moment would have just wanted this  to be a warm encounter of course the  reason for the sussex family's trip  across the pond to celebrate the queen's  platinum jubilee honoring 70 years of  service on the throne but the 96 year  old monarch has already run into some  conflicts for events in her honor e.t  has learned the queen will not attend  the platinum party nor the epson derby  on saturday but is expected to watch it  at windsor castle the queen won't be  going to tomorrow's horse races at epsom  and she won't be at the party at the  palace here but there is a hope that she  will get to meet her namesake lily bett  on her first birthday clearly family  always comes first  [Music]  you
 

